# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lumen
# the desktop and its login screen. LiquidDesktop's own dependencies come with liquid-desktop-git, and build.sh
# adds every optional dependency listed in its PKGBUILD (newest commit) below this list, so nothing here needs updating
# when LiquidDesktop adds one.
liquid-desktop-git
lumen-installer
greetd
cage
xorg-server
xorg-xinit
xorg-xrdb
xorg-xinput
xorg-xrandr
xorg-xsetroot
xorg-xprop
xorg-setxkbmap
xorg-xwayland
xsettingsd
picom
electron43
kvantum
sassc
# boot screen and terminal greeting
plymouth
fastfetch
# graphics: open-source drivers for every card, plus NVIDIA's driver (open kernel modules: GTX 16 / RTX 20 and
# newer), so the live session runs properly on NVIDIA cards. The installer keeps it only when it's chosen.
nvidia-open
nvidia-utils
nvidia-settings
nvidia-prime
libva-nvidia-driver
opencl-nvidia
mesa
mesa-utils
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
vulkan-nouveau
intel-media-driver
libva-intel-driver
xf86-video-amdgpu
xf86-video-nouveau
xf86-video-qxl
pciutils
# Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware (the releng list's linux-firmware pulls these in too; listed so they can't go
# missing). Intel AX2xx, MediaTek MT7921/MT7922 and Realtek RTW89 cover current laptops, including the
# Lenovo Legion Pro 5 16IRX8H, whatever card it shipped with.
linux-firmware-intel
linux-firmware-mediatek
linux-firmware-realtek
linux-firmware-atheros
linux-firmware-broadcom
wireless-regdb
wpa_supplicant
